libpkgreconcile-apply(3)

# NAME

libpkgreconcile-apply - project completed package application into reconciliation state

# DESCRIPTION

*libpkgreconcile-apply* translates completed *libpkgapply* rejected-object
consequences into package-independent *libpkgreconcile* pending values.

It projects the exact managed target, accepted operation plan, physical
application attempt, canonical package path, retained side, rejected-object
store identity, and rejected-object record identity already established by
completed application evidence.

# TARGET REFERENCES

The provider *libpkgreconcile-apply/managed-target/v1* carries the exact 32-byte
*managed_target_identity* digest.

# REJECTED-OBJECT LOCATORS

The provider *libpkgreconcile-apply/rejected-object/v1* carries exactly 64 bytes:
the 32-byte *rejected_object_store_identity* followed by the 32-byte
*rejected_object_record_identity*.

Consumers should use the public decoder instead of interpreting these bytes.
No filesystem pathname is encoded.

# BOUNDARY

The library does not open rejected objects, persist inventories, inspect
installed package state, infer ownership, choose reconciliation dispositions,
or coordinate transactions.

# SEE ALSO

libpkgapply(3), libpkgreconcile(3)
